  "seoBody": "<div class=\"key-takeaways\"><strong>Key takeaways</strong><ul><li>UK food businesses must have a food safety management system based on the seven HACCP principles under Regulation (EC) 852/2004</li><li>Safer Food Better Business is the FSA's ready-made HACCP-based system for small caterers, with a daily diary and safe-method sheets</li><li>The HACCP plan is built once with a competent person; the daily diary and corrective-action records are the part staff complete every shift</li><li>Monitoring records for temperature, cleaning, deliveries and allergens are what an EHO inspects</li><li>An app does not write your HACCP plan; it captures that the daily controls happened, with photos and timestamps</li></ul></div><h2>What HACCP actually requires</h2><p>HACCP stands for Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points. Its seven principles are: conduct a hazard analysis; identify the critical control points; establish critical limits; establish monitoring procedures; establish corrective actions; establish verification; and establish documentation and record-keeping. Under Regulation (EC) 852/2004, every UK food business must put in place and maintain a system based on these principles, proportionate to its size and risk.</p><p>The first steps are the plan, built once with a competent person. The rest is daily practice: monitor the controls, correct problems, verify the system works, keep the records. An app does not write the plan or replace the competent person. It makes the daily monitoring and corrective-action records easy to complete and hard to skip.</p><h2>Safer Food Better Business explained</h2><p>For small caterers, the Food Standards Agency publishes Safer Food Better Business (SFBB), a ready-made system that meets the HACCP requirement without a bespoke plan. It groups controls into safe methods covering cross-contamination, cleaning, chilling and cooking, and provides a daily diary where you record that the checks were done and note anything that went wrong.</p><p>SFBB is genuinely simpler, but the diary still has to be completed daily and kept up to date. A blank or backfilled diary helps nobody on inspection day. Quickler turns the SFBB diary into a WhatsApp conversation: the day's checks arrive as messages, staff reply as they work, and the record builds itself. Check the current SFBB pack on the FSA website for your business type; this is not legal advice.</p><h2>Where the daily HACCP checks land</h2><h3>1. Cooking and reheating</h3><p>Cooking aims for a safe core temperature, commonly 75C or an equivalent time and temperature combination, and reheating to a safe temperature. These are recorded readings, not a memory.</p><h3>2. Chilling and hot holding</h3><p>Chilled storage at or below 8C, hot holding at or above 63C, and safe cooling of cooked food are core critical control points, logged against each unit.</p><h3>3. Cross-contamination</h3><p>Separation of raw and ready-to-eat food, clean-as-you-go, and colour-coded equipment controls the biggest kitchen hazard. The record shows the controls were followed.</p><h3>4. Allergens</h3><p>Under Natasha's Law and the Food Information Regulations, the 14 major allergens must be managed and prepacked for direct sale food labelled in full. Allergen handling is part of the daily HACCP record.</p><h2>Corrective action is the record that matters</h2><p>When a check is within limits, the record is routine. When a reading is out of limit, the corrective action is the record that matters most: what you found, and what you did about it. A fridge reading 11C with a note that stock was moved and the unit called in is a record that protects you. A blank line is not. Quickler prompts for the reading, flags an out-of-limit value, and captures the corrective action in the same conversation.</p><h2>Comparison: the main options</h2><ul><li><strong>Paper SFBB diary</strong> - the FSA pack. Free and familiar, but easy to backfill and invisible across sites.</li><li><strong>iAuditor</strong> - general inspection app, from around 19 pounds per seat per month. App install and template setup required.</li><li><strong>FoodDocs, Navitas</strong> - food-safety-specific HACCP apps. Capable, but another app and login, priced per seat or per site.</li><li><strong>Quickler</strong> - WhatsApp workflow, 20 pounds per active user per month, dormant users free. Only pay for who works. Free tier of 20 reports a month, everything unlimited on a paid account. Runs in WhatsApp, no install or training.</li></ul><p>Pricing is approximate and shifts. Check each vendor's current rates directly before you commit.</p><div class=\"callout\"><strong>Honest note:</strong> an app does not write your HACCP plan or make the kitchen safe, the competent person and the practice do. But without the daily records you have no due-diligence defence and no confidence-in-management score. Quickler captures the diary with photo and timestamp and gives head office a live view across sites. <a href=\"/pages/help/index.html#contact-form-section\">Ask us</a> if that distinction matters for your firm.</div><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>What is a HACCP checklist app?</h3><p>It is a tool that captures the daily monitoring and corrective-action records your HACCP-based food safety management system requires: temperatures, cleaning, deliveries, allergen controls. Options range from the paper SFBB diary, to generic audit apps, to conversation-based tools like quickler that run the daily diary over WhatsApp so there is no app to install.</p><h3>Is HACCP a legal requirement in the UK?</h3><p>Yes. Regulation (EC) 852/2004 requires every UK food business to put in place, implement and maintain a food safety management system based on HACCP principles. Small caterers can meet this with the FSA's Safer Food Better Business pack. The system must be proportionate to the business. Check current FSA guidance for your business type; this is not legal advice.</p><h3>Does an app write my HACCP plan?</h3><p>No. The HACCP plan, identifying your hazards, critical control points and limits, should be built with a competent person and reflect your specific menu and premises. Quickler does not write the plan or replace that competence. It captures the daily monitoring and corrective-action records the plan requires, with photos and timestamps head office can see.</p><h3>Can I run my SFBB diary over WhatsApp?</h3><p>Yes. Quickler's workflows run over the WhatsApp Business API. The day's checks arrive as messages in your team's existing WhatsApp chat, staff reply with text, a voice note or a photo, and the diary record generates automatically with a timestamp. No separate app or login is required, and quickler manages the WhatsApp Business API account on the firm's behalf.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/food-safety-audit-app-uk.html\">Food safety audit app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/kitchen-temperature-log-app-uk.html\">Kitchen temperature log app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/due-diligence-food-hygiene-uk.html\">Food hygiene due diligence records</a></li></ul>",
